  "title": "The Ramanujan-Nagell theorem",
  "abstract": "Formalizes the Ramanujan-Nagell theorem, proving that the Diophantine equation x^2 + 7 = 2^n has exactly the five positive-integer solutions (|x|, n) = (1, 3), (3, 4), (5, 5), (11, 7), (181, 15).",
